{"seq":15,"trial_id":"shared-bot-scope-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-installer-labelled-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-14T13:17:05.808Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"7930074bc83fad5399b49d093effee5f126be81c5cb5a709b223a740cc0e177d","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes (the team-north digests):\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md, 5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their SMS bay assignments at kiosk check-in. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the 04:00 shift got through the gate fine. The note also has a follow-up to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). It says Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift, and that it went to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nMoss's other two QFL notes, the 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal check-in, don't have any ticket numbers.\n\nBefore #4419 goes in the weekly notes, check it: Marcus's 14 Jul 2025 handoff note (members/marcus-lindqvist/notes/2025-07-14-marcus-q2-expansion-wrap.md), which isn't one of Moss's, calls #4419 \"Gate 3 printer lag\" (a delay on BOL printouts). That doesn't match the cheat sheet's scanner description, and the cheat sheet has no date, so I can't tell which is right. The ticket file under accounts/ or Marcus would know."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
